  "worked_solution": "The function $G(t)$ models the growth rate for the bacteria $t$ hours since the sample was put in the Petri dish.\n\nThus, the growth rate of the bacteria culture after $6$ hours is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}G(6) & =100\\cdot {2}^{0.5(6)} \\\\  & =100\\cdot {2}^{3} \\\\  & =100\\cdot 8 \\\\  & =800.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the growth rate of the bacteria is $800$ bacteria per hour.",
